{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9e27b850c46b8934", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# MOVA: Towards Scalable and Synchronized Video-Audio Generation\narXiv: 2602.08794\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We develop MOVA, a synchronized video-audio generation model with an asymmetric dual-tower architecture that leverages pre-trained video and audio generation models.\n  2. We design a fine-grained audio-video captioning pipeline to produce high-quality bimodal training data at scale.\n  3. By scaling video-audio training, we achieve continuous improvements in synchronization performance across both modalities.\n\nTags: related-work, we develop, we design, by scaling\n===\n# Audio-Omni: Extending Multi-modal Understanding to Versatile Audio Generation and Editing\narXiv: 2604.10708\nAuthors: Zeyue Tian, Binxin Yang, Zhaoyang Liu, Jiexuan Zhang, Ruibin Yuan, Hubery Yin, Qifeng Chen, Chen Li, Jing Lv, Wei Xue, Yike Guo\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose Audio-Omni, the first unified framework for audio understanding, generation, and editing across general sound, music, and speech, featuring a decoupled architecture that bridges a frozen MLLM with a trainable DiT via a hybrid conditioning mechanism.\n  2. We introduce AudioEdit, a large-scale, high-quality dataset comprising over one million curated instruction-guided audio editing pairs constructed through a hybrid pipeline of real-world data mining and programmatic synthesis.\n  3. Extensive experiments demonstrate that Audio-Omni outperforms prior unified models and achieves competitive or superior results compared to specialized expert models across a broad range of tasks.\n  4. Audio-Omni exhibits remarkable inherited capabilities from the frozen MLLM, such as knowledge-augmented generation and zero-shot cross-lingual control, highlighting a path toward intelligent and versatile generative audio systems.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/音频标记-融合, TTS, TTS/功能-语音编辑\n===\n# WavFlow: Audio Generation in Waveform Space\narXiv: 2605.18749\nAuthors: Feiyan Zhou, Luyuan Wang, Shoufa Chen, Zhe Wang, Zhiheng Liu, Yuren Cong, Xiaohui Zhang, Fanny Yang, Belinda Zeng\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. WavFlow introduces a simplified architecture that synthesizes high-fidelity audio directly in raw waveform space using waveform patchify, x-prediction flow matching, and specialized signal preprocessing to eliminate the need for audio tokenizers.\n  2. An automated data curation pipeline is developed to harvest large-scale, high-quality video-text-audio triplets to address the sensitivity of direct waveform modeling to data quality and scale.\n  3. Empirical validation demonstrates competitive results on VGGSound and AudioCaps benchmarks, proving that end-to-end raw waveform generation matches or exceeds the performance of established latent-based methods.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "6fd9fdf1-b774-46c0-b355-0709c229ad96", "uuid": "34a3ebbe-a20c-4f78-b976-55362a902fdf", "timestamp": "2026-07-28T08:19:40.921Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# MOVA: Towards Scalable and Synchronized Video-Audio Generation\narXiv: 2602.08794\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We develop MOVA, a synchronized video-audio generation model with an asymmetric dual-tower architecture that leverages pre-trained video and audio generation models.\n  2. We design a fine-grained audio-video captioning pipeline to produce high-quality bimodal training data at scale.\n  3. By scaling video-audio training, we achieve continuous improvements in synchronization performance across both modalities.\n\nTags: related-work, we develop, we design, by scaling\n===\n# Audio-Omni: Extending Multi-modal Understanding to Versatile Audio Generation and Editing\narXiv: 2604.10708\nAuthors: Zeyue Tian, Binxin Yang, Zhaoyang Liu, Jiexuan Zhang, Ruibin Yuan, Hubery Yin, Qifeng Chen, Chen Li, Jing Lv, Wei Xue, Yike Guo\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose Audio-Omni, the first unified framework for audio understanding, generation, and editing across general sound, music, and speech, featuring a decoupled architecture that bridges a frozen MLLM with a trainable DiT via a hybrid conditioning mechanism.\n  2. We introduce AudioEdit, a large-scale, high-quality dataset comprising over one million curated instruction-guided audio editing pairs constructed through a hybrid pipeline of real-world data mining and programmatic synthesis.\n  3. Extensive experiments demonstrate that Audio-Omni outperforms prior unified models and achieves competitive or superior results compared to specialized expert models across a broad range of tasks.\n  4. Audio-Omni exhibits remarkable inherited capabilities from the frozen MLLM, such as knowledge-augmented generation and zero-shot cross-lingual control, highlighting a path toward intelligent and versatile generative audio systems.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/音频标记-融合, TTS, TTS/功能-语音编辑\n===\n# WavFlow: Audio Generation in Waveform Space\narXiv: 2605.18749\nAuthors: Feiyan Zhou, Luyuan Wang, Shoufa Chen, Zhe Wang, Zhiheng Liu, Yuren Cong, Xiaohui Zhang, Fanny Yang, Belinda Zeng\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. WavFlow introduces a simplified architecture that synthesizes high-fidelity audio directly in raw waveform space using waveform patchify, x-prediction flow matching, and specialized signal preprocessing to eliminate the need for audio tokenizers.\n  2. An automated data curation pipeline is developed to harvest large-scale, high-quality video-text-audio triplets to address the sensitivity of direct waveform modeling to data quality and scale.\n  3. Empirical validation demonstrates competitive results on VGGSound and AudioCaps benchmarks, proving that end-to-end raw waveform generation matches or exceeds the performance of established latent-based methods.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
